    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0332" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H.01/7–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-11T19:00:00-04:00">July 11, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Dept has noted widely quoted press reports of statement attributed to
                    Marshal Tito on July 8 accusing Greek forces of firing across Greek-Yugoslav
                    border “to provoke us”. Similar accusations published previously in Belgrade
                    have also come to Dept’s attention.</p>
                <p>Please inform FonOff that no information from other sources has <pb facs="0333"
                        n="321" xml:id="pg321"/> been received by Dept to substantiate these
                    statements and this Govt will appreciate any data Yugoslav authorities can
                    furnish.</p>
                <p>Sent to Belgrade, repeated to London, Moscow and Athens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
